[{:db/id 17592186198646 :question/problem "![](images/df/df0ffdd8bfb94ece82926411bfddb3affc85e802807a36cb2e8ee9b9b727633c.png)\n\nA plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the $x$-axis and the lines $y=x$ and $y=2-x$, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is $\\lambda (x,y)=3x+2.$ Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $y=1.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type II region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,y\\le x\\le 2-y\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/d1/d1241b56d482f24cc06d51a9aaecbc623805df0a76739201e5cbe6974e2e9c6f.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $y=1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-1|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{2-y}(3x+2)|y-1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{2-y}(3x+2)(y-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-2y+1)[{\\int }_{y}^{2-y}3x+2\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-2y+1){[\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+2x]}_{x=y}^{x=2-y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-2y+1)[\\frac{3}{2}(2-y)^{2}+2(2-y)-(\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+2y)]\\text{d}y \\\\  & =10{\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-2y+1)(1-y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =10{\\int }_{0}^{1}1-3y+3{y}^{2}-{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =10{[y-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+{y}^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =10(1-\\frac{3}{2}+1-\\frac{1}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186194507 :answer-field/correct 17592186194510 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198416 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5254f44e-1aee-5d92-b378-2e98dcb05199"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198647 :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,3\\le x\\le 5,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1\\}.$\nFind the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $y=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point on $D$ and the line $y=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 1=2.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{M}{2}|y-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{M}{2}(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}({\\int }_{3}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot [x]_{3}^{5}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}(y-2)^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(5-3)(\\frac{1}{3}(1-2)^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(0-2)^{3}) \\\\  & =M(-\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186194513 :answer-field/correct 17592186194517 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-5254f44e-1aee-5d92-b378-2e98dcb05199" :question/id #uuid "5254f44e-1aee-5d92-b378-2e98dcb05199" :question/math-academy-id "q-163619" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1\\}.$\nFind the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $y=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point on $D$ and the line $y=-2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y+2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=1\\cdot 2=2.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=-2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{M}{2}|y+2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{M}{2}(y+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}({\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{-1}^{1}(y+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot [x]_{1}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}(y+2)^{3}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(2-1)(\\frac{1}{3}(1+2)^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(-1+2)^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(9-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{13M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-845cdc46-a35a-5586-a626-09720ae6b110"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-845cdc46-a35a-5586-a626-09720ae6b110" :answer-field/id #uuid "845cdc46-a35a-5586-a626-09720ae6b110" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7faf4b7f-4f51-54e5-8676-2aff35a9aba8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b4815fe0-0696-5b13-b4e7-7c49e55ee3fd" "answer-c351d508-c06d-56b5-81fc-74bc138267ed" "answer-7faf4b7f-4f51-54e5-8676-2aff35a9aba8" "answer-e4cb05b1-5665-5f7f-bb6c-6b8055b9e402" "answer-dfeaebde-f303-5342-a31a-0aa1900de703"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4815fe0-0696-5b13-b4e7-7c49e55ee3fd" :answer/id #uuid "b4815fe0-0696-5b13-b4e7-7c49e55ee3fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c351d508-c06d-56b5-81fc-74bc138267ed" :answer/id #uuid "c351d508-c06d-56b5-81fc-74bc138267ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7faf4b7f-4f51-54e5-8676-2aff35a9aba8" :answer/id #uuid "7faf4b7f-4f51-54e5-8676-2aff35a9aba8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13M}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4cb05b1-5665-5f7f-bb6c-6b8055b9e402" :answer/id #uuid "e4cb05b1-5665-5f7f-bb6c-6b8055b9e402" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2M}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfeaebde-f303-5342-a31a-0aa1900de703" :answer/id #uuid "dfeaebde-f303-5342-a31a-0aa1900de703" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{M}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198418 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3a407e50-1493-5ac2-abfc-afeed102785c" "question-bff66772-3aa9-52e4-ae38-3aff93ff5b7b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3a407e50-1493-5ac2-abfc-afeed102785c" :question/id #uuid "3a407e50-1493-5ac2-abfc-afeed102785c" :question/math-academy-id "q-163652" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1\\}.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to the square of its distance from the $y$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k{x}^{2},$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}k{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k({\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =k\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{2}\\cdot [y]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{3}(8-0)(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8k}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k{x}^{2}=\\frac{3M}{8}{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3M}{8}{x}^{2}|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3M}{8}{x}^{2}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{8}({\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{8}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}-{x}^{4}+\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{2}\\cdot {[y]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{8}\\cdot (\\frac{32}{5}-16+\\frac{32}{3})\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{8}\\cdot \\frac{16}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a5556ed2-662d-582b-a0da-d02820904882"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a5556ed2-662d-582b-a0da-d02820904882" :answer-field/id #uuid "a5556ed2-662d-582b-a0da-d02820904882" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ce166fcb-1dfc-519c-a85d-161ea72636a9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c76013eb-2e60-5dc8-b1fd-86c086d4bcfe" "answer-ea2a98ac-fbb8-5412-baa1-04362a35b51a" "answer-6abdd6fd-84fe-5787-9074-401ecc94520e" "answer-ce166fcb-1dfc-519c-a85d-161ea72636a9" "answer-54b7a4ed-6a62-5958-af18-fb40a86462b1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c76013eb-2e60-5dc8-b1fd-86c086d4bcfe" :answer/id #uuid "c76013eb-2e60-5dc8-b1fd-86c086d4bcfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{128M}{45}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea2a98ac-fbb8-5412-baa1-04362a35b51a" :answer/id #uuid "ea2a98ac-fbb8-5412-baa1-04362a35b51a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15M}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6abdd6fd-84fe-5787-9074-401ecc94520e" :answer/id #uuid "6abdd6fd-84fe-5787-9074-401ecc94520e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{29M}{45}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce166fcb-1dfc-519c-a85d-161ea72636a9" :answer/id #uuid "ce166fcb-1dfc-519c-a85d-161ea72636a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2M}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54b7a4ed-6a62-5958-af18-fb40a86462b1" :answer/id #uuid "54b7a4ed-6a62-5958-af18-fb40a86462b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6M}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bff66772-3aa9-52e4-ae38-3aff93ff5b7b" :question/id #uuid "bff66772-3aa9-52e4-ae38-3aff93ff5b7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-163664" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-3\\le x\\le 0,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\}.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to the square of its distance from the $x$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k{y}^{2},$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{1}^{3}k{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k({\\int }_{-3}^{0}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{1}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =k\\cdot [x]_{-3}^{0}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{3}(0-(-3))(27-1) \\\\  & =26k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k{y}^{2}=\\frac{M}{26}{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{M}{26}{y}^{2}|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{M}{26}{y}^{2}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{26}({\\int }_{-3}^{0}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{1}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{26}\\cdot {[\\frac{(x-2)^{3}}{3}]}_{-3}^{0}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{26}\\cdot (-\\frac{8}{3}+\\frac{125}{3})\\cdot (9-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{26}\\cdot 39\\cdot \\frac{26}{3} \\\\  & =13M.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-641b9e4b-4711-52d7-948a-1033dbe4f079"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-641b9e4b-4711-52d7-948a-1033dbe4f079" :answer-field/id #uuid "641b9e4b-4711-52d7-948a-1033dbe4f079" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c82691e9-9f25-55f2-9f79-61a4e0f60f25" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c82691e9-9f25-55f2-9f79-61a4e0f60f25" "answer-d4bef6bd-0aec-5f69-bb41-4ec8057c0acb" "answer-c0f6f1aa-4c77-51d1-8803-77e7ade1835f" "answer-5f3cd980-48ea-571b-9b45-60baf14b36fc" "answer-9d4ed41d-46b1-5cfa-ac2b-42be83590f8b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c82691e9-9f25-55f2-9f79-61a4e0f60f25" :answer/id #uuid "c82691e9-9f25-55f2-9f79-61a4e0f60f25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13M" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4bef6bd-0aec-5f69-bb41-4ec8057c0acb" :answer/id #uuid "d4bef6bd-0aec-5f69-bb41-4ec8057c0acb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2M" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0f6f1aa-4c77-51d1-8803-77e7ade1835f" :answer/id #uuid "c0f6f1aa-4c77-51d1-8803-77e7ade1835f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3M" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f3cd980-48ea-571b-9b45-60baf14b36fc" :answer/id #uuid "5f3cd980-48ea-571b-9b45-60baf14b36fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5M" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d4ed41d-46b1-5cfa-ac2b-42be83590f8b" :answer/id #uuid "9d4ed41d-46b1-5cfa-ac2b-42be83590f8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7M" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-eb4e0c90-e4bf-5334-a41e-c9dcbc6b2de0" :activity/id #uuid "eb4e0c90-e4bf-5334-a41e-c9dcbc6b2de0" :activity/title "Moments of Inertia of Laminas About Other Axes" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048585 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-af1f1335-4b99-5b58-9b75-fe6f46cf00ad" "step-07466f53-e252-509d-8a34-a405145acef5" "step-bf1ba95f-9b2b-5cae-8cac-39eec0a7a2c4" "step-75f7502b-d79d-5e16-8da0-486fac5f9f4b" "step-f0e756d4-4310-5dd8-bca5-e3e7d601cc8a"] :activity/first-step "step-af1f1335-4b99-5b58-9b75-fe6f46cf00ad" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-af1f1335-4b99-5b58-9b75-fe6f46cf00ad" :step/id #uuid "af1f1335-4b99-5b58-9b75-fe6f46cf00ad" :step/content 17592186198646 :step/next "step-07466f53-e252-509d-8a34-a405145acef5" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-07466f53-e252-509d-8a34-a405145acef5" :step/id #uuid "07466f53-e252-509d-8a34-a405145acef5" :step/content 17592186198647 :step/next "step-bf1ba95f-9b2b-5cae-8cac-39eec0a7a2c4" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-bf1ba95f-9b2b-5cae-8cac-39eec0a7a2c4" :step/id #uuid "bf1ba95f-9b2b-5cae-8cac-39eec0a7a2c4" :step/content "question-5254f44e-1aee-5d92-b378-2e98dcb05199" :step/next "step-75f7502b-d79d-5e16-8da0-486fac5f9f4b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-75f7502b-d79d-5e16-8da0-486fac5f9f4b" :step/id #uuid "75f7502b-d79d-5e16-8da0-486fac5f9f4b" :step/content "question-3a407e50-1493-5ac2-abfc-afeed102785c" :step/next "step-f0e756d4-4310-5dd8-bca5-e3e7d601cc8a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f0e756d4-4310-5dd8-bca5-e3e7d601cc8a" :step/id #uuid "f0e756d4-4310-5dd8-bca5-e3e7d601cc8a" :step/content "question-bff66772-3aa9-52e4-ae38-3aff93ff5b7b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
